The attached image, Figure 2 from the npj Vaccines 2017 paper, demonstrates that Nano-11 nanoparticles are retained at the injection site and gradually cleared in mice. Panel A shows in vivo fluorescence imaging over 21 days, indicating Nano-11 (Alexa Fluor 647-labeled) remains localized to the intramuscular injection site with diminishing signal over time. Panel B, depicting excised internal organs and injection sites at day 21, confirms that Nano-11 did not widely distribute systemically. Panel C quantifies the injection site fluorescence, showing an initial increase in intensity followed by a progressive decrease, with significant clearance by day 14 and day 21 compared to day 2.